From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the night light warms the pointer on a monitor with
 no gamma

On a DisplayLink dock (evdi) the CRTC has no gamma table, so viz warms
the frame through the display color matrix, and the cursor plane skips
it. A white pointer on that warm screen looked blue. On every other
monitor the CRTC's ramp warms the cursor plane with the rest.

- OzonePlatform::SetDomicileCursorTint takes a display's night light
  gains, with its rectangle. The broker sends the matrix's diagonal with
  each matrix.
- DrmCursor warms the pointer's bitmaps by the gains of the display its
  window shows (TintedCursorBitmaps: each encoded channel by the gain's
  2.2nd root, as a ramp would), and sends it again when that display's
  gains change.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
